--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SURFACE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SuspenseProgressBoundary is the web progress-tracking Suspense boundary wrapped around every code-split
route (web/src/components/feedback/SuspenseProgressBoundary.tsx). The web component wraps <Suspense> so
that while a lazy chunk downloads the fallback is shown and the global progress bar activates
(globalProgress.start() in the internal ProgressTrackingFallback's useEffect), and when the real
component resolves the fallback is swapped for the children and the bar deactivates (the effect cleanup
/ returned stop()). The controller it drives (web/src/lib/globalProgress.ts) jumps to 8 on the first
start, trickles asymptotically toward 80 (+max(1, remaining*0.15) every 120 ms), stacks concurrent
consumers (the bar stays active until the last stop), snaps back to 0 on the last stop, replays the
current state to every new subscriber, and returns an idempotent stop.

It is ANONYMOUS and purely presentational: the web source has NO titles, labels, i18n keys, charts,
maps, or data hooks, and NO loading/empty/error/stale/offline branches — only the two states the native
port reproduces: pending/suspended (show the fallback; hold a consumer on the global channel) and
resolved (show the children; release the consumer). Fabricating empty/error/stale/offline chrome the
web source lacks would be parity drift, so — per the VisuallyHidden / withAiFeature anonymous-surface
precedent — none was invented. The "loading" state IS the pending branch (the caller's fallback) and is
fully rendered. Evidence is in the doc-comments.

Native decomposition (per-surface sub-namespace SuspenseProgressBoundarySurface to avoid CS0101 with
the generically-named GlobalProgress* types, the same isolation pattern VisuallyHidden uses):
  - SuspenseProgressBoundary.Model.cs     Registration (Slug "SuspenseProgressBoundary"),
                                          GlobalProgressSnapshot (web __getGlobalProgressStateForTests),
                                          PII-safe SuspenseProgressBoundaryDiagnostics (view.opened).
  - SuspenseProgressBoundary.Source.cs    GlobalProgressListener, IGlobalProgress + GlobalProgress
                                          (Shared singleton, TrickleTarget/Initial/IntervalMs consts,
                                          initial jump, asymptotic trickle, consumer stacking, idempotent
                                          stop, subscriber replay, listener-error isolation, thread-safe);
                                          IGlobalProgressTicker + TimerGlobalProgressTicker (the real
                                          System.Threading.Timer trickle, web setInterval); NoOpGlobalProgress
                                          (inert fallback for isolated hosts, the NoOpAnnouncer precedent).
  - SuspenseProgressBoundary.ViewModel.cs SuspenseProgressBoundaryViewModel — the ProgressTrackingFallback
                                          bridge: IsPending edge acquires/releases a consumer (start/stop),
                                          reflects live IsProgressActive/Progress, idempotent Dispose.
  - SuspenseProgressBoundary.cs           SuspenseProgressBoundary : ContentControl — Fallback /
                                          ResolvedContent / IsPending dependency properties; swaps the shown
                                          child on the pending edge; drives the channel through the view-model;
                                          transparent (AccessibilityView.Raw) nameless Group automation peer;
                                          emits view.opened once on Loaded; marshals view-model changes to the
                                          UI thread.

The interface member IGlobalProgressTicker.Stop() was renamed StopTicking() because CA1716 (reserved
VB keyword 'Stop') is an error under the app project's TreatWarningsAsErrors.

